  <!-- The club platform -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header section-header--center">
        <h2 class="section-heading">Run it across your whole club</h2>
        <p class="section-subheading">A scoreboard paired to every sheet, your leagues and rosters in it, your bonspiels planned in it, and the scores on screens around the building.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="feature-card-title">A scoreboard on every sheet</h3>
          <p>Pair each sheet's scoreboard once with a six character code. The club portal then shows every sheet at a glance — what is live, which scoreboards are online, and which need an update. Scoring still works if the internet does not, and syncs when it comes back.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="feature-card-title">Leagues and real team names</h3>
          <p>Set up each league with its draw times and teams, or import the whole roster from a CSV. On league nights the scoreboard offers that night's league and puts both team names up on their rock colors, so players can check that whoever set it up got it right.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="feature-card-title">Bonspiels, start to finish</h3>
          <p>Plan a spiel on a draw board, or fill one in from a knockout or pools template. Brackets and pool standings work themselves out as results come in, and each sheet's scoreboard offers that sheet's next game with the teams already filled in.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="feature-card-title">A warm room screen</h3>
          <p>Every sheet on one TV, sized to fill whatever screen you put it on, with the end, the league and both teams on their rock colors. Add your club's name and logo to the title bar. Leave it running for the season.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="feature-card-title">A score bug for your stream</h3>
          <p>A transparent overlay you drop into OBS as a browser source. It shows the teams, scores, hammer and end, scales to fit your layout, and hides itself between games. A preview mode makes it easy to place while the ice is empty.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="feature-card-title">Scores on your website</h3>
          <p>A read-only API serves live and finished games, leagues and bonspiels to your club's site, with documentation and a test page. Or have every finished game post itself to a Slack or Discord channel, in a message you write.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

